+## 0.38.1-calendar-single-attempt - local maintenance patch
+
+- Calendar: serialize an explicitly supplied `--guests-can-modify=false` as JSON false on create rather than relying on the API default.
+
+- Calendar: disable HTTP retries for event inserts, including inserts that request attendee notifications. An error may follow a committed event; surface it rather than creating another event or repeating invitations. Normal base-transport authentication remains unchanged.
+
 ## 0.38.1 - 2026-08-25
 
 - Gmail: send exact prebuilt RFC822 messages with verified sender/account guards, normalized thread IDs, and content-safe offline dry runs. (#1032, #1029) — thanks @higginz777.
